#
# CODEOWNERS assigns reviewers to pull requests based on file paths.
#
# How it works:
#   * The LAST matching pattern wins. Put specific paths after the
#     catch-all `*` rule -- not before it. This is the opposite of
#     .gitignore, where the first match wins.
#   * This file must live on the repository's default branch to take
#     effect. Editing it on a feature branch has no immediate impact.
#   * Every listed owner must have write access to the repository, or
#     the entry is silently ignored for review-request purposes.
#   * CODEOWNERS requests reviews. It does NOT block merges unless a
#     branch protection rule or ruleset requires "Require review from
#     Code Owners" to pass.
#
# Format reference:
#   https://docs.github.com/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# Conventions:
#   * Patterns are POSIX-style, matched against paths from the repo root.
#     A leading `/` anchors to the root; a trailing `/` matches a directory
#     and everything under it.
#   * `*` in the middle of a segment matches within that segment; `**`
#     matches across segments.
#   * Keep one owner per section while the project has a single maintainer.
#     The explicit entries are here so the intent survives if that changes.
#   * Do not remove an entry because it duplicates the default. If the
#     default owner ever changes, the explicit entries are what preserve
#     review coverage on the paths that matter.

